WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
- Tell everyone what you created and why.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.300
- So, on a recent trip to
a toy store, I saw that

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.730
you know, no dolls resembled
my students' hearing devices.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.560
They have hearing aids
and cochlear implants.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.084
So, I went home and
crafted them myself for

00:00:14.084 --> 00:00:17.360
to have my students resemble
the toys that they play with.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.501
- That is amazing.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:20.820
(audience applauding)
Is it so?

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.140
You know a lot of people
would just stop right there

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.050
and go, "well it just doesn't exist",

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.150
but you like went the extra mile.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.103
I know teachers don't have a
lot of spare time in general

00:00:28.103 --> 00:00:29.100
- (laughs) Yes.
- My momma was a teacher,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.600
so the fact that you went above.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.722
- Thank you so much
- And beyond, it's amazing.

00:00:31.722 --> 00:00:32.555
- I really appreciate that.

00:00:32.555 --> 00:00:35.360
- So Genesis had 115 followers
when she posted this tweet

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.793
but within 24 hours, the
post had 30,000 retweets

00:00:37.793 --> 00:00:40.440
and 150,000 likes.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.160
So Genesis, how did your
students react to the doll?

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.010
- They loved them.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.630
Those with cochlear implants reached for

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.910
the dolls with cochlear implants

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.140
and those with hearing aid reached for

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.040
those with hearing aids.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.850
So it really shows how
much they identify with

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.683
the toys that they play with.

00:00:51.683 --> 00:00:52.516
- Yeah, they got to see.

00:00:52.516 --> 00:00:54.130
There was like one of my
favorite parts of being

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.940
I got to this film called ugly dolls

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.340
and it's like the thing about the dolls

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.320
was like everybody kind
of related to one of them

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.880
and they weren't your normal doll.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.200
And I though that was brilliant
what you did for them.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.162
- Thank you so much.

00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:05.995
- And it's so special.

00:01:05.995 --> 00:01:06.828
And are they still playing with the dolls,

00:01:06.828 --> 00:01:07.661
how did they react?

00:01:07.661 --> 00:01:09.270
- Yes, we have tea
parties, birthday parties.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.390
They make cakes for them.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:11.560
- [Kelly] That's so good.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.410
- It's so much fun.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:13.870
They have never been put down since.

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.780
- Man, representation is so important

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.060
in every facet of what am saying it

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.569
for metaphorically everyway.

00:01:19.569 --> 00:01:22.035
(audience applauds)
It is so important.

00:01:22.035 --> 00:01:23.590
Well, thank you so much.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:24.530
- Thank you so much.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.330
- I admire your ingenuity and
the passion for your students.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.990
Teachers like you really
do make a difference.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.190
You make kids feels
special and it really does

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.110
and can change the
trajectory of their life.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.790
So, thank you so much.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:36.623
- Thank you for having me.

00:01:36.623 --> 00:01:37.640
(audience applauding)

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.360
- Well, let's bring up
my first guest girl.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.560
You know her from Glee, Christopher
Guest's brilliant movies

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.910
and now from the Marvelous Mrs Maisel

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.150
which you can watch on
Amazon prime videos.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.250
So say hello to a woman who has become

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.176
a fast friend of the
show, Jane Lynch, y'all.

00:01:52.176 --> 00:01:53.627
(audience applauding)

00:01:53.627 --> 00:01:56.210
(upbeat music)

00:01:59.669 --> 00:02:00.919
You're so fine.

00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:03.760
- Good to see you

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.677
(audience applaud)

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.830
- Come on over.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:15.770
- I love this set.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:19.419
- I am so appreciative,
you came back again.

00:02:19.419 --> 00:02:20.420
- I did, thank you for inviting me.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.980
- That means you must not have hated it.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.090
- No, I enjoyed it so much.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:24.280
- Okay, good.
- Yes.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.970
- I was like, that's the goal.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.904
- Well, you're isn't she the best at this?

00:02:27.904 --> 00:02:29.866
(audience applauding)

00:02:29.866 --> 00:02:30.699
You're so great.

00:02:30.699 --> 00:02:32.470
- You're very nice.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:34.320
You actually, actually, Genesis you are,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.340
are you deaf in your right ear?

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.173
- I am, Where is Genesis?

00:02:36.173 --> 00:02:37.007
- Yeah, Genesis was just
telling about the dolls.

00:02:37.007 --> 00:02:38.350
Are they not kinda cool?

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.010
- I just think it's so wonderful.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:40.843
It's the sweetest thing

00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:43.210
I am deaf in my right
ear but one of the things

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.870
that I love watching on YouTube

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.050
is when they put the cochlear implant

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.150
in like a baby for the very first time.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:49.983
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:49.983 --> 00:02:51.680
- Wow, and they hear their mother's voice

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:52.803
for the very first time.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:52.803 --> 00:02:55.560
- That's one of the most
moving things in the world.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.320
- And it's also one of the
things we take advantage of.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.380
Like everybody that has it

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.768
and you don't have to
worry that, you know.

00:02:59.768 --> 00:03:00.601
- Right, exactly.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.200
- It's like really be grateful.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.780
- Well, I am really grateful too.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.530
I have one ear and it's bionic.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.660
It's so not gonna wanna--

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.493
- It's stepped up to the play.

00:03:08.493 --> 00:03:11.620
- It has totally made up for
the one that doesn't work so.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.250
And it's been all my life so I didn't have

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.030
to have like that adjustment period.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.190
- Yeah, and music is important to you.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.023
- It is.

00:03:17.023 --> 00:03:18.230
